	<!--
		!vip - the VIP mouse menu. Driven by VIPCore/Hud/VipMenu.cs. The first of our layouts that takes input
		through PanoramaManager's click channel; the shape follows the /rank menu (Ranks/ranks_menu.xml).

		Replaces the "VIP Menu" center menu, "You have set FOV to 90" and, for players without VIP,
		"You don't have access to this command!" - they get the group comparison instead.

		CONTRACT (VipMenu.cs must match)
		  RootPanelId = "VipMenuRoot"   RevealClass = "show"   CloseButtonId = "vm_close"   RowCount = 0
		  CaptureInput = true           HideHud = None         SharedText = false

		The root is the full screen (a light dim while open); the card sits in the middle.

		POOLS (generous on purpose: the plugin fills them from whatever VIP modules are loaded, and a bigger
		pool later means a new workshop upload)
		  vm_r0..vm_r5          settings rows, each with 8 option buttons or one "go" button
		  vm_t0..vm_t3          perk tiles
		  vc_r0..vc_r7          comparison rows, vc_h0..vc_h3 group columns

		BUTTONS (PanelAction.Button, by id)
		  vm_close                     close (the library handles it)
		  vm_rN_oM                     option M of row N (FOV 60, TAG ON, ...)
		  vm_rN_go                     a "go" row: another plugin's menu (!music, !sky) or a module's own menu

		DIALOG VARIABLES
		  vm_tag vm_gname vm_until_a vm_until_b vm_until_c
		  vm_tN_k vm_tN_v                    tile label, value
		  vm_rN_k vm_rN_oM_t vm_rN_go_t      row label, option text, go text
		  vc_intro vc_cta vc_hN vc_rN_k vc_rN_cM

		CLASSES THE SERVER TOGGLES
		  vm                 g-vip g-premium g-supreme g-none | perm | soon
		  vm_member, vm_compare                 hidden (one page or the other)
		  vm_fill            p0 .. p20          (5% a step, a clip)
		  vm_tN              hidden, off
		  vm_rN              hidden, kind-go
		  vm_rN_oM           hidden, sel, locked
		  vc_hN              hidden, g-vip g-premium g-supreme g-none
		  vc_rN              hidden
		  vc_rN_cM           hidden, no
	-->
